<title>CANADA: Consumers' Gas files for C$750 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Consumers' Gas files for C$750 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Consumers' Gas Co Ltd said on Wednesday it had filed a prospectus to issue from time to time up to C$750 million of unsecured medium-term notes with maturities of one year or more.</p>
<p>The notes will be offered by Nesbitt Burns Inc, RBC Dominion Securities Inc, CIBC Wood Gundy Securities Inc, Levesque Beaubien Geoffrion Inc, ScotiaMcLeod Inc and TD Securities Inc, under an agreement signed on October 7.</p>
<p>Consumers' Gas is owned 85 percent by IPL Energy Inc.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
